#TETHERVERSE FRONTEND — PRODUCTION
#
# Every value here is public or a server-side URL. There is no secret in this file,
# and that is deliberate: the frontend holds no database credential, so there is
# nothing here worth leaking.
#
#   cp env.prod .env.production.local

# ── Tetherverse API ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Do not prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_: that inlines it into the
# client bundle and publishes the backend's address to every player.
#
# <<< UNRESOLVED: the API has never been deployed. >>>
# Set this to the public HTTPS address of the running Tetherverse API. Until then
# every /api route returns 502.
#
# Must be https in production: the frontend calls this server-side carrying the
# Excel Play bearer, so a plaintext hop would expose that token in transit.
TETHERVERSE_API_URL=https://REPLACE_ME-with-the-deployed-tetherverse-api-host

# ── Excel Play sign-in ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Browser-facing by design: this one really is in the client bundle.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EXCEL_AUTH_FRONTEND_URL=https://auth.excelmec.org

# ── Launcher bridge ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The iframe handshake only accepts an auth token from an origin listed here, so a
# wrong or missing value means the game falls back to standalone Excel sign-in
# rather than trusting a stranger's frame. This is a security control, not a
# convenience setting: list every origin that legitimately embeds this app, and
# nothing else. No wildcards.
#
# This is the LAUNCHER, not this app: it is the frame being embedded, which is the
# opposite direction from the NEXT_PUBLIC_SUMMIT_JACK_URL the launcher sets.
NEXT_PUBLIC_LAUNCHER_ORIGIN=https://REPLACE_ME-with-the-deployed-launcher-origin

# ── Deliberately absent ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY / SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
#   The `tetherverse` schema is not exposed to the Supabase Data API, so no API key
#   can reach it. The Tetherverse API service holds the Postgres connection string
#   instead. A key here would be dead weight in the client bundle, and this file is
#   committed: it would publish a live credential that the architecture has
#   deliberately made useless.
#
# EXCEL_ACCOUNTS_API_URL
#   Moved to the backend. This app forwards /api/excel-auth/exchange rather than
#   calling the accounts backend itself.
#
# NODE_ENV
#   Set by `next build` and `next start`. Setting it here has no effect.
#
# MONGODB_URI
#   Unused. Kept commented in .env.local so a rollback stays one edit away.